{"sentence": "Under the Chapter V text, a transfer of personal data to a third country or international organisation may take place on the basis of a Commission decision that the destination ensures an adequate level of protection, and such a transfer shall not require any specific authorisation.", "label": "supported", "rationale": "This accurately summarizes Article 45(1), which permits transfers based on a Commission adequacy decision and specifies that such transfers do not require specific authorisation.", "excerpt": "A transfer of personal data to a third country or an international organisation may take place where the Commission has decided that the third country... ensures an adequate level of protection. Such a transfer shall not require any specific authorisation."}
{"sentence": "The text sets out the impact as follows:", "label": "no_rad", "rationale": "This is an introductory framing sentence that does not present a verifiable factual claim.", "excerpt": null}
{"sentence": "- General transfer condition: Article 44 states that any transfer of personal data which are undergoing processing or are intended for processing after transfer to a third country or to an international organisation shall take place only if, subject to the other provisions of this Regulation, the conditions laid down in this Chapter are complied with by the controller and processor, including for onward transfers of personal data from the third country or an international organisation to another third country or to another international organisation.", "label": "supported", "rationale": "This sentence is a faithful restatement of Article 44's general principle for transfers, including the requirement to comply with Chapter V conditions and its applicability to onward transfers.", "excerpt": "Any transfer of personal data which are undergoing processing or are intended for processing after transfer to a third country or to an international organisation shall take place only if... the conditions laid down in this Chapter are complied with by the controller and processor, including for onward transfers of personal data from the third country or an international organisation to another third country or to another international organisation."}
{"sentence": "All provisions in this Chapter shall be applied in order to ensure that the level of protection of natural persons guaranteed by this Regulation is not undermined.", "label": "supported", "rationale": "This is the concluding sentence of Article 44 and matches the text exactly.", "excerpt": "All provisions in this Chapter shall be applied in order to ensure that the level of protection of natural persons guaranteed by this Regulation is not undermined."}
{"sentence": "- Basis for transfer: Article 45(1) states that a transfer of personal data to a third country or an international organisation may take place where the Commission has decided that the third country, a territory or one or more specified sectors within that third country, or the international organisation in question ensures an adequate level of protection.", "label": "supported", "rationale": "This matches Article 45(1) describing the basis for transfers on an adequacy decision.", "excerpt": "A transfer of personal data to a third country or an international organisation may take place where the Commission has decided that the third country, a territory or one or more specified sectors within that third country, or the international organisation in question ensures an adequate level of protection."}
{"sentence": "It adds: `Such a transfer shall not require any specific authorisation.`", "label": "supported", "rationale": "This directly quotes the final sentence of Article 45(1).", "excerpt": "Such a transfer shall not require any specific authorisation."}
{"sentence": "- Assessment criteria: When assessing the adequacy of the level of protection, the Commission shall, in particular, take account of:", "label": "supported", "rationale": "This reproduces the lead-in of Article 45(2) concerning assessment criteria.", "excerpt": "When assessing the adequacy of the level of protection, the Commission shall, in particular, take account of the following elements:"}
{"sentence": "  - the rule of law, respect for human rights and fundamental freedoms, relevant legislation, both general and sectoral, including concerning public security, defence, national security and criminal law and the access of public authorities to personal data, as well as the implementation of such legislation, data protection rules, professional rules and security measures, including rules for the onward transfer of personal data to another third country or international organisation which are complied with in that country or international organisation, case-law, as well as effective and enforceable data subject rights and effective administrative and judicial redress for the data subjects whose personal data are being transferred;", "label": "supported", "rationale": "This item is a faithful reproduction of Article 45(2)(a).", "excerpt": "the rule of law, respect for human rights and fundamental freedoms, relevant legislation, both general and sectoral... including rules for the onward transfer of personal data... case-law, as well as effective and enforceable data subject rights and effective administrative and judicial redress for the data subjects whose personal data are being transferred"}
{"sentence": "  - the existence and effective functioning of one or more independent supervisory authorities in the third country or to which an international organisation is subject, with responsibility for ensuring and enforcing compliance with the data protection rules, including adequate enforcement powers, for assisting and advising the data subjects in exercising their rights and for cooperation with the supervisory authorities of the Member States; and", "label": "supported", "rationale": "This item mirrors Article 45(2)(b) regarding supervisory authorities.", "excerpt": "the existence and effective functioning of one or more independent supervisory authorities in the third country or to which an international organisation is subject, with responsibility for ensuring and enforcing compliance with the data protection rules, including adequate enforcement powers, for assisting and advising the data subjects in exercising their rights and for cooperation with the supervisory authorities of the Member States"}
{"sentence": "  - the international commitments the third country or international organisation concerned has entered into, or other obligations arising from legally binding conventions or instruments as well as from its participation in multilateral or regional systems, in particular in relation to the protection of personal data.", "label": "supported", "rationale": "This item reproduces Article 45(2)(c) concerning international commitments.", "excerpt": "the international commitments the third country or international organisation concerned has entered into, or other obligations arising from legally binding conventions or instruments as well as from its participation in multilateral or regional systems, in particular in relation to the protection of personal data"}
{"sentence": "- Adoption and review: After assessing the adequacy of the level of protection, the Commission may decide, by means of implementing act, that a third country, a territory or one or more specified sectors within a third country, or an international organisation ensures an adequate level of protection within the meaning of paragraph 2.", "label": "supported", "rationale": "This paraphrases Article 45(3) authorising the Commission to adopt an implementing act to decide adequacy.", "excerpt": "The Commission, after assessing the adequacy of the level of protection, may decide, by means of implementing act, that a third country, a territory or one or more specified sectors within a third country, or an international organisation ensures an adequate level of protection within the meaning of paragraph 2 of this Article."}
